  "releaseNotes": "- GLSL: only emit `nonuniformEXT` (and require `GL_EXT_nonuniform_qualifier`) for dynamic descriptor-array indexing when the target uses descriptor sets (Vulkan, `createDescriptorSets = true`). On the GL backend there is no such extension and a dynamically-uniform index needs no qualifier, so bindless storage-buffer arrays (`X[i].data[j]`) and sampler/image arrays now compile on GL instead of failing with `undefined variable \"nonuniformEXT\"`",
